# rpi-utils
PKG_SUFFIX=".20260914"
PKG_URL="https://github.com/raspberrypi/utils/archive/ebc4a56bac3a896d5c14e56fe27dcd6cb36dd373.tar.gz"
### The tools need no library of their own: they talk to the kernel and to the firmware directly
PKG_DEPS=
BUILD_PROCESS=cmakebuild
PKG_MAKETARGETS="all,install/strip"
### The userspace tools of the Raspberry Pi, what Raspberry Pi OS ships as raspi-utils: vcgencmd,
### vcmailbox and vclog ask the firmware through the mailbox of /dev/vcio (nothing of the deprecated
### userland repository and its /opt/vc is involved), pinctrl reads and sets the pins (it replaces
### raspi-gpio), raspinfo collects the output of all of them, eeptools reads and writes the EEPROM of
### a HAT. RPI_UTILS_TOOLS is the list of subdirectories of the sources prebuild.sh puts into the top
### level CMakeLists. Left out: the helpers that only make sense on a build host (otamaker, ovmerge,
### splashasm), the libraries of hardware this framework builds for no board of (piolib is the PIO of
### the RP1, rpieepromab the A/B eeprom of the Pi 5) and the two tools that would drag a library in
### for themselves (rpi-gpu-usage wants ncurses, rpifwcrypto gnutls)
RPI_UTILS_TOOLS="eeptools pinctrl raspinfo vcgencmd vclog vcmailbox"
### WITH_DT_TOOLS=1 adds the device tree tools, which link libfdt (variants/option/dt-tools)
WITH_DT_TOOLS=${WITH_DT_TOOLS:-0}
### The libraries of the sources are internal to their tool (libgpiolib of pinctrl, libdtovl of
### dtmerge) and their install rules name the ARCHIVE artifact only: built shared, nothing would be
### installed for them and the programs would keep a dangling DT_NEEDED. They are built static and
### linked in, and the .a is a development file the installer leaves out of the image
PKG_OVERRIDESHARED=0
PKG_OVERRIDESTATIC=1
